{#
  T-7.06 — one item in the customer-stories feed.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.stories.story-card' with { story: item } %}

  Parameters:
    story   required — one entry from the story collection

  WHY THIS IS A PARTIAL AND NOT A LOOP BODY. T-7.07 opens the same item in a
  modal, and the owner's B6 ruling is explicit that the story view is a view of
  *this* item rather than a second thing that happens to look like it. Keeping
  the card in its own file is what lets the modal reuse the tag row and the media
  well instead of transcribing them.

  THE CARD IS NOT A CONTROL, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Nothing here is focusable:
  pressing a story opens the T-7.07 modal, which does not exist yet, and a card
  that looks pressable and does nothing is worse than a plain image for someone
  who cannot see that it is dead — the same call T-4.01 made about quick view.
  **T-7.07 adds the trigger.** Until then this is exactly what the feed artboard
  draws: a picture with its tags beneath it.

  THE SHAPE IS A MERCHANT FIELD BECAUSE NOTHING ELSE KNOWS IT. A masonry grid is
  made of images of different heights, and the theme is handed a URL with no
  dimensions attached — so either the box is reserved from a stored ratio or it
  is not reserved at all, and zero CLS is a requirement here, not an aspiration.
  Three shapes cover the artboard; the value feeds `--card-media-ratio`, which
  T-2.15's card shell already reads.
#}
{% set story_ratios = {
    'square':   '1 / 1',
    'portrait': '3 / 4',
    'tall':     '2 / 3'
} %}
{% set story_ratio = story_ratios[story.shape|default('portrait')]|default('3 / 4') %}
{% set story_tags = story.tags is defined and story.tags is not empty ? story.tags|split(',') : [] %}

<li class="story-card">
    <div class="card__media story-card__media" style="--card-media-ratio: {{ story_ratio }}">
        <img src="{{ story.image }}"
             alt="{{ story.alt|default('') }}"
             loading="lazy"
             decoding="async">
    </div>

    {% if story.brand or story_tags|length %}
        <ul class="story-card__tags" aria-label="{{ trans('theme.stories.tags_label') }}">
            {#
              The brand comes first, which in Arabic puts it at the right-hand end
              of the row — the artboard's order on every card in the feed.

              `<bdi>` and not a bare `<span>`: brand names are Latin runs inside an
              RTL list, and T-1.04's rule is that bidi isolation goes on an inline
              element around the run and never on the block that contains it.
            #}
            {% if story.brand %}
                <li class="story-card__tag"><bdi>{{ story.brand }}</bdi></li>
            {% endif %}

            {% for tag in story_tags %}
                {% if tag|trim %}
                    <li class="story-card__tag">{{ tag|trim }}</li>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}
</li>
